    :row/run-id
    :row/check-id
    :row/verdict
    :row/artifact
    :row/at
    :row/author
    :row/sha],
   :optional [:row/notes :row/deposited-by],
   :enums #:row{:verdict #{:green :red :typed-absence}},
   :rules
   ["exactly one row per (:row/run-id, :row/check-id) -- a second, divergent verdict for the same pair is a conflict the append API refuses, and an identical replay is :already-present"
    ":row/check-id must be a member of the declared :ledger/check-catalogue -- the catalogue below is the only enumeration of check ids, so a typo cannot invent a check"
    ":row/artifact must RESOLVE: a repository-relative path (optionally suffixed :LINE or :LINE-LINE) naming a file that exists under the pointer root. A verdict with no readable artifact is not evidence"
    ":row/verdict :typed-absence requires non-blank :row/notes naming what the run store did not hold -- the honest store rule, mechanised; an absence that says nothing is indistinguishable from a check that never ran"
    ":row/seq is unique, starts at 1, and is contiguous and ascending -- rows are appended, never rewritten or removed"
    ":row/at is an ISO-8601 instant (parseable by java.time.Instant), so rows form a time series"
    ":row/sha is SHA-256 over the previous row's :row/sha (\"genesis\" for the first) followed by this row's authored fields serialised canonically (all keys but :row/sha, in sorted-key order). :ledger/head-sha equals the last row's :row/sha, or nil for an empty ledger"]},
